# ChimeraX Script: S438T Local Energy Minimization
# Targets the S1 binding pocket residues around Threonine 438 (TM10)
#
# Usage:
#   File > Open > select this script, OR
#   Command: open scripts/S438T_Minimization_Workflow.cxc
#
# Input:  data/structures/5i6z_A_S438T.pdb
# Output: data/structures/5i6z_A_S438T_minimized.pdb

# 1. Load the S438T mutant structure
open data/structures/5i6z_A_S438T.pdb

# 2. Add hydrogens and assign charges (required for energy minimization)
addh
addcharge

# 3. Select the S1 binding pocket residues
#    Core contact residues from Coleman (2016) and Andersen (2009):
#      Y95, D98           -- TM1 (H-bond partners of the drug amino group)
#      A169, I172         -- TM3 (hydrophobic contacts)
#      S277               -- TM6
#      T438, S439         -- TM10 (mutation site + adjacent)
#    Plus local TM10 context (435-442) to allow backbone relaxation
select :95,98,169,172,277,435-442

# 4. Freeze the rest of the protein to preserve global fold
freeze ~:95,98,169,172,277,435-442

# 5. Energy minimization
#    100 steps steepest descent to remove clashes, then 200 conjugate gradient
#    to refine side-chain geometry around THR438
minimize nsteps 100 cgsteps 200 stepsize 0.02 interval 10

# 6. Post-minimization: verify THR438 geometry
select :438
show :438 atoms
label :438 text "{0.name} {0.number}" height 1.5

# 7. H-bond analysis around the mutated site
hbonds :435-442 reveal true

# 8. Save the minimized structure
save data/structures/5i6z_A_S438T_minimized.pdb format pdb models #1

# 9. Report RMSD of the minimized pocket vs input (quantify relaxation)
rmsd #1:95,98,169,172,277,435-442 to #1:95,98,169,172,277,435-442
